traceability.evidence:
Story file is a concrete spec with explicit acceptance criteria and requirements:
- docs/stories/025.0-DEV-CATCH-ANNOTATION-POSITION.story.md (content matches the story provided, including ACs and REQ-* items).,CatchClause dual-position detection and fallback logic are implemented in the branch annotation helper:
- src/utils/branch-annotation-helpers.ts
  - DEFAULT_BRANCH_TYPES includes "CatchClause" (existing requirement IMPL-CATCHCLAUSE-HANDLER):
    export const DEFAULT_BRANCH_TYPES = [
      "IfStatement", "SwitchCase", "TryStatement", "CatchClause", "ForStatement", "ForOfStatement", "ForInStatement", "WhileStatement", "DoWhileStatement",
    ] as const;
  - gatherBranchCommentText now has CatchClause-specific behavior:
    const beforeComments = sourceCode.getCommentsBefore(node) || [];
    const beforeText = beforeComments.map(commentToValue).join(" ");
    if (node.type === "CatchClause") {
      if (/@story\b/.test(beforeText) || /@req\b/.test(beforeText)) {
        return beforeText;   // prefers before-catch when annotations present
      }
      const getCommentsInside: unknown = (sourceCode as any).getCommentsInside;
      if (node.body && typeof getCommentsInside === "function") {
        try {
          const insideComments = (getCommentsInside as (_node: any) => any[])(node.body) || [];
          const insideText = insideComments.map(commentToValue).join(" ");
          return insideText || beforeText;  // fallback to inside-catch when before-catch has no annotations
        } catch {
          return beforeText;
        }
      }
      return beforeText;
    }
    return beforeText;
  - This implements REQ-DUAL-POSITION-DETECTION (checks before AND inside), REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC (falls back to inside when before has no annotations), and REQ-POSITION-PRIORITY (returns beforeText when it already contains @story/@req).,Auto-fix for CatchClause is adjusted to insert inside the catch body, not before the catch keyword:
- src/utils/branch-annotation-helpers.ts, getBranchAnnotationInfo:
  const text = gatherBranchCommentText(sourceCode, node);
  const missingStory = !/@story\b/.test(text);
  const missingReq = !/@req\b/.test(text);
  let indent = sourceCode.lines[node.loc.start.line - 1].match(/^(\s*)/)?.[1] || "";
  let insertPos = sourceCode.getIndexFromLoc({ line: node.loc.start.line, column: 0 });
  if (node.type === "CatchClause" && node.body) {
    const bodyNode: any = node.body;
    const bodyStatements: any[] | undefined = Array.isArray(bodyNode.body) ? bodyNode.body : undefined;
    const firstStatement: any | undefined = bodyStatements && bodyStatements.length > 0 ? bodyStatements[0] : undefined;
    if (firstStatement && firstStatement.loc && firstStatement.loc.start) {
      const firstLine = firstStatement.loc.start.line;
      const innerIndent = sourceCode.lines[firstLine - 1].match(/^(\s*)/)?.[1] || "";
      indent = innerIndent;
      insertPos = sourceCode.getIndexFromLoc({ line: firstLine, column: 0 });
    } else if (bodyNode.loc && bodyNode.loc.start) {
      const blockLine = bodyNode.loc.start.line;
      const blockIndent = sourceCode.lines[blockLine - 1].match(/^(\s*)/)?.[1] || "";
      const innerIndent = `${blockIndent}  `;
      indent = innerIndent;
      insertPos = sourceCode.getIndexFromLoc({ line: blockLine, column: 0 });
    }
  }
  return { missingStory, missingReq, indent, insertPos };
- reportMissingStory/reportMissingReq then use insertPos/indent to insert annotations. This satisfies REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX by targeting the first statement inside the catch block, which Prettier will preserve.,Unit tests explicitly target this story and its requirements for CatchClause behavior:
- tests/utils/branch-annotation-catch-position.test.ts
  - File header:
    * @story docs/stories/025.0-DEV-CATCH-ANNOTATION-POSITION.story.md
    * @supports ... REQ-DUAL-POSITION-DETECTION REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC REQ-POSITION-PRIORITY REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX
  - Tests:
    - "[REQ-DUAL-POSITION-DETECTION] prefers before-catch annotations when present":
      * sourceCode mock returns beforeComments with @story/@req and commentsInside with a different @story.
      * node.type = "CatchClause".
      * Asserts that gatherBranchCommentText(...) contains the before-catch story and req, proving position priority and preservation of existing behavior.
    - "[REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC] falls back to inside-catch annotations when before-catch is missing":
      * commentsBefore is empty; commentsInside contain @story and @req.
      * Asserts that returned text contains the inside-catch story/req, proving fallback detection.
    - "[REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC] returns before-catch text when getCommentsInside is not available":
      * SourceCode mock omits getCommentsInside; commentsBefore has annotations.
      * Asserts the returned text still contains the before-catch annotations (safe fallback).,Auto-fix insert position for CatchClause is covered by a dedicated test:
- tests/utils/branch-annotation-catch-insert-position.test.ts
  - Header:
    * @story docs/stories/025.0-DEV-CATCH-ANNOTATION-POSITION.story.md
    * @supports ... REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX
  - Test: "[REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX] inserts annotations at the first statement inside the catch body"
    * lines represent:
      try {
        doSomething();
      }
      catch (error) {
        handleError(error);
      }
    * context.getSourceCode() mock implements lines, getCommentsBefore() => [] and getIndexFromLoc(...).
    * node is a CatchClause whose body contains an ExpressionStatement at line 5.
    * reportMissingAnnotations(context, node, storyFixCountRef) is called.
    * Assertions:
      - insertTextBeforeRange called once.
      - range passed to insertTextBeforeRange equals [index(line 5, column 0), same], i.e. before first statement in catch body.
      - inserted text starts with "  " (inner indentation from line 5).
    * This confirms auto-fix inserts inside the catch body with correct indentation.,Existing rule-level tests for require-branch-annotation still pass, ensuring no regressions for catch and other branch types:
- tests/rules/require-branch-annotation.test.ts
  - Has a valid case for catch with annotations before the catch keyword:
    name: "[REQ-BRANCH-DETECTION] valid catch with annotations",
    code: `/* @story ... */\n/* @req ... */\ntry { ... }\n/* @story ... */\n/* @req ... */\ncatch (error) { ... }`,
  - Has an invalid case:
    name: "[REQ-BRANCH-DETECTION] missing annotations on try-catch blocks",
    code: try/catch with no annotations, and expects missingAnnotation errors for both try and catch and an auto-fix inserting a @story before the try.
  - These tests still use only before-catch annotations (no inside-catch examples) but they continue to pass after the new helper changes, indicating no regression for existing behavior on catch or other branch types.,Jest test run shows the new story-specific utility tests are executed and passing:
