- No test file exercises require-branch-annotation against real code where annotations are inside the catch block body due to Prettier formatting; only the helper is unit-tested with mocked getCommentsInside.,Rule documentation has not been updated to describe dual valid positions for catch annotations or Prettier compatibility (violating the "Documentation" acceptance criterion and DoD):
- docs/rules/require-branch-annotation.md
  - Rule details say: "This rule checks for JSDoc or inline comments immediately preceding significant code branches and ensures both `@story` and `@req` annotations are present." (emphasis on preceding only).
  - Options and examples mention only the standard before-branch comment placement (e.g., before an if statement).
  - There is no mention that CatchClause annotations may also appear as the first comments inside the catch block, and no section on Prettier compatibility.
- No separate documentation file or section provides Prettier-specific guidance for this rule.,The story's Definition of Done explicitly calls for additional artifacts that are not present:
